# Secrets. .env.example is the only env file that belongs in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# uv and virtualenvs. uv.lock is committed on purpose for reproducible CI.
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Local model and data artifacts (P1)
*.gguf
*.safetensors
models/
data/

# Vendored docs corpus and batch payloads. Cloned on demand, never committed.
# training/artifacts/ IS committed: manifest, dataset, golden set, spend ledger.
training/.scratch/
# Review batches are a byte-for-byte re-slice of review_export.jsonl, which is
# committed. `golden review-export` asserts the concatenation, so the batches are
# regenerable and committing both would duplicate 1.08 MB.
training/artifacts/review_batches/
# Rendered P1.2 training splits: ~23 MB, and ~95% of it is corpus chunk text
# repeated across examples. `corpus fetch` + `corpus parse` rebuild that text for
# free and deterministically (11.3 s and 3.4 s), so the repo carries the split
# *definition* instead: dataset_manifest.json holds per-split question_ids plus a
# sha256 of each rendered file, and `dataset verify` proves a rebuild is
# byte-identical. Committing the rendered text also means committing upstream
# documentation verbatim, which is how a Grafana placeholder token in the Grafana
# docs tripped GitHub push protection on 2026-08-02.
# NOTE: this does NOT back up the teacher answers, which cost $2.89 and live only
# in Postgres. See PROGRESS section 6.
training/artifacts/dataset/
# Scratch output of `dataset restore`. Disposable by design: it exists only to be
# digest-compared against the manifest and must never be what training reads.
training/artifacts/restore_check/
# Adapter weights and raw console logs. `*.safetensors` is already ignored above;
# this also covers adapter_config.json and the checkpoint dirs.
# `probe_v1_losses.jsonl` is deliberately NOT ignored -- it is the measurement the
# learning-rate decision rests on, and it is a few KB.
training/artifacts/adapters-*/
training/artifacts/*_console.log
# Staged copy of the selected checkpoint. Byte-identical to a file under
# adapters-v1/ by construction -- stage_selected_adapter.sh asserts it -- so
# committing it would duplicate 19 MB of weights that are already ignored.
# SELECTED.json inside it is regenerated by the same script.
training/artifacts/adapters-v1-selected/

# Judge response caches. SQLite, binary, and pure derived state: the cache is
# keyed on (case, output, rubric, judge version) and any entry it holds can be
# recomputed by re-running the judge. A StubJudge cache additionally holds no
# information at all -- the verdicts are constants.
#
# The reason to be explicit rather than rely on *.sqlite: this file is what makes
# a re-run of a *paid* judge free, so someone will eventually be tempted to
# commit it to share the savings. Don't. It is keyed on model outputs, so it is
# only valid for one model version, and a stale entry silently scores a new model
# with an old verdict. CI restores it from actions/cache, which expires; that is
# the correct lifetime for it.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
training/artifacts/**/judge.sqlite

# Built suites: a rendering of the committed golden_set.jsonl, verified
# byte-identical on rebuild (`build-suite`, ~1 s). Same rule as the dataset
# splits -- commit the definition and a digest, not the rendering. The sha256
# lives in p13/gguf_manifest.json so a rebuild is provable.
training/artifacts/**/suite.json

# Terraform (P2)
# .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed on purpose: it is the provider version pin.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
# Backend config names a tenancy-specific bucket and namespace. Not secret, but
# not portable either; the S3 credentials themselves live in ~/.aws/credentials.
backend.hcl
!backend.hcl.example
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Capacity retry logs. Machine-local run history, not project state; the
# measured attempt count and elapsed time go in DECISIONS.md instead.
infra/terraform/logs/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
